{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013148-building-santa-claus-2e","id":1013148,"title":"Building Santa Claus 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-06T07:29:44-08:00","id":1013148,"title":"Building Santa Claus 2e","content":"So how would you build Santa Claus 2e CoD?<br /> <br /> How would you use Changeling, Mage, Demon, Werewolf, Vampire, Promethean, Beast rules repectively to build Santa Claus?<br /> <br /> Maybe a Changeling Wizen Maker, a Collector Raptor who atones one a year for his actions by gift giving, Thyemus Free Council Mage who took the words spirit of christmas too literally, a pack of 12 werewolves with Santa Claus as their totem, Lancea Sactum Vampire who is convinced he is Saint Nick, a demon who made a pack with a mall santa only to find out when he called the pact in, that he'd effectly claimed the real Santa Claus identity, a Prommy was built from Christmas snow one day and came alive (okay that one is more frosty the snow man). Just some ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T08:19:39-08:00","id":1013174,"title":"","content":"We need <b>Santa Claws</b> - Predator Bodhisattva werewolf Elodoth from Iron Masters under Yule spirit totem that sate his Sacred Hunt needs by tracking children around a world once a year and giving them gifts. Catch is that no Half Moon gives anything for free. And when you are big and grown up, better watch out when people sings 'Santa Claws is coming to town...' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-06-2016, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T08:26:10-08:00","id":1013178,"title":"","content":"Reighnhell wrote up <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=787167#post787167\"><b>Santa</b></a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=788492#post788492\"><b>Krampus</b></a> as Horrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T08:37:42-08:00","id":1013188,"title":"","content":"Santa and Krampus (and his other variations and related mythical figures) could well be Fae titles. Fairies aren't always malicious, but &quot;watching children at all times and filling their socks with coal&quot; sound like the kind of lunatic crap that a Fairy might do. The North Pole could be his Arcadian Realm, and the Elves his Changeling slave-labor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T10:17:33-08:00","id":1013255,"title":"","content":"All excellent ideas forumites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T10:45:04-08:00","id":1013263,"title":"","content":"While Santa seems very powerful-changeling to me, I vaguely like the idea of him being a beast, with The Krampus being his Horror. Who would ever expect the kindly old man who climbs down your chimney to leave gifts and the terrifying monster that attacks you in nightmares when you're naughty are the same entity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T12:25:48-08:00","id":1014410,"title":"","content":"Santa Claus is a powerful Seer of the Throne who enslaves human children by bribing them into behaving through promise of material reward, all while reminding them that they are constantly watched and judged. A fun crossover between Mammon and the Eye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}